# Which repository secrets the API reads, and the config key each one carries.
#
#   <config key the API answers to>=<repository secret holding the value>
#
# The two names cannot be the same, which is the only reason this file exists:
# cpconfigs reads env vars with "." as the nesting delimiter, so the API wants
# `chat.service.tagSalt` — and a GitHub secret name cannot contain a dot.
# render-env.sh does the rename and writes the result to .env.backend, which the
# backend loads whole. docker-compose.yaml therefore names no secret at all.
#
# This file is also the routing rule. A secret listed here goes to the backend
# and to nothing else; every other secret goes to .env, which Caddy loads. So a
# secret Caddy needs takes no edit anywhere, and one the API reads takes exactly
# one line, here — which is the least that can be written down, because the
# config key it maps to is genuinely new information.
#
# A secret named here but not set in the repository is skipped with a note
# rather than written empty, and the API then applies its own default or
# refuses to boot, whichever that setting calls for.

# Salts the per-sender chat tag. Anyone holding it can recompute a sender's tag
# from a guessed address, which is the one thing the tag prevents. Changing it
# renames every sender at once, so treat it as permanent.
chat.service.tagSalt=CHAT_TAG_SALT

# Signs the session tokens that gate the Click RPC. Anyone holding it can mint a
# token the API accepts. Empty refuses the boot: the mint and the click check
# each derive a signer from it, so an invented one would differ between them.
session.secret=SESSION_SECRET

# The Turnstile widget's secret half. Unused while session.turnstile.enabled is
# false, which is why it is allowed to be unset.
session.turnstile.secret=TURNSTILE_SECRET
